# core.autocrlf=true is set on this machine, and this repo has no attributes file, so git
# rewrites LF -> CRLF on every checkout. For .sh that is not cosmetic: a CRLF script dies with
# `$'\r': command not found` under any invocation that is not Git Bash — which is how the test
# gate and the VPS run them. preflight.sh and deploy_vps.sh both had to be repaired for exactly
# this reason on 2026-08-08; without this file the next checkout silently reintroduces it.
*.sh text eol=lf
# Same reasoning, and the reason the rule cannot just be "*.sh": git hooks carry no extension.
# They are run by sh, so a CRLF checkout breaks them exactly the same way — and a broken
# post-commit hook fails silently, which is how the graph froze on 2026-08-09.
scripts/githooks/* text eol=lf
